cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  nlm_synth: neutral landscape models with prescribed marginal
  distributions
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file, along with the NLMpy references below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Amin
    given-names: Shadman
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShadmanAmin/nlmpy_synth"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for generating synthetic rasters that combine a
  controlled amount of spatial structure, drawn from a neutral
  landscape model, with an observed value distribution supplied by
  the user. Because spatial structure and the marginal distribution
  are varied independently, the package can isolate how landscape
  heterogeneity statistics such as Moran's I and variance respond to
  changes in observation scale.
keywords:
  - neutral landscape model
  - Perlin noise
  - remote sensing
  - NDVI
  - spatial heterogeneity
  - scaling
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
